A||N||5||Monkeyman||3rd Brake Light Mounting---Need Help!||||1||
Z||000000||Monkeyman||04-17-2000||03:14 PM||||I'd like to mount the 3rd brake light out of the Monkeymobile ('86 SC) into the Grape Ape ('85 GT).  The correct holes are in the roof, but there aren't any nuts (?) welded to the roof like the Monkeymobile.  Any suggestions other than removing the roof panel and welding nuts up there?  (I neither have access to a welder nor do I want to remove the roof panel.)  Now that most of the housework is done, I'd like to start getting some stuff done to the car.  (But not today--worked 36 out of the last 42 hours.  Time for bed now!)||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||04-17-2000||03:28 PM||||There are some pop rivet type dodads the have threads in them. Check J.C. Whitney to see what I'm talking about but they should be available locally. Or file the holes square and push in some of those nylon inserts, you'll find some on the headlight brackets on your parts car. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||04-17-2000||07:29 PM||||try plastic screw rivits. look in the rest of the hardware at the store. should come 2-4 to a pack for about 1.50<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||BAM-BAM||04-17-2000||08:46 PM||||     Hey Monkey, I just picked up a third light and I am going to install it in my 85GT<BR>probably this weekend. If you get yours done first let me know at: BartlettDS@LVCM.COM. I would be interestedd in knowing how you did it.<P> Thanx, BAM-BAM  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000004||Monkeyman||04-18-2000||09:35 AM||||I'll let you know.  I think I'll try it after work tomorrow.  Thanx for all of the advice.||||reg||1
